== Musical instruments ==

Baliscan music employs diverse instruments derived from multiple traditions:

=== Indigenous instruments ===

* '''Yvyra-pu''' — Kurupiran [[W:Frame drum|frame drum]] used in ceremonial contexts
* '''Kãsere''' — End-blown [[W:Flute|flute]] of hollow reed; gives name to "forest" terminology
* '''Mba'e-puku''' — Percussion [[W:Rattle|rattle]] used in rituals

=== Mesogean instruments ===

* '''Guitarro baliscano''' — Modified [[guitar]] with extended neck; standard ensemble instrument
* '''Acordeão do vale''' — [[W:Accordion|Accordion]] associated with rural folk traditions
* '''Bandurria baliscana''' — Adapted [[W:Bandurria|bandurria]] used in traditional ensembles

=== Kaftian-derived instruments ===

* '''Djembe baliscano''' — Adapted [[W:Djembe|djembe]] with local construction modifications
* '''Kora of Araucaria''' — Regionally adapted [[kora]] tradition
* '''Balafon-isla''' — Island-modified [[balafon]] (wooden xylophone)

=== Bayani/Imfezzan instruments ===

* '''Oud baliscano''' — Locally constructed [[oud]]
* '''Darbuka''' — Retained in Mozbayán and Imfezzan communities
* '''Qanun''' — Used in Bayani-influenced urban music

